ly what Daenerys and her Dothraki  horde unleashed on King's Landing in the  fifth episode of the final season it  seemed out of character until you  remember that Daenerys made a similar  pact with the Dothraki back in season  six and again Marty looks like she has  more than kept both of those promises  after losing her husband Daenerys made  several attempts to find armies and  benefactors to back her in the war to  come  and during Thrones the second season she  ran afoul of the Warlocks of Qarth who  stole her dragons and lured her into the  terrifying and mystical house of the  undying to get them back naturally  Daenerys charged into the temple to  track down her children and experienced  a number of visions along the way seeing  everything from her late husband Drogo  and their lost child to a battered and  seemingly destroyed Iron Throne standing  in an empty and ravaged throne room it  seems as if Daenerys is surrounded by  snow but thanks to the aftermath of  King's Landing in the wake of her  ruthless and murderous siege it's clear  that her vision has come true and it's  not snow but ashes many viewers always  believed that the snow was a sign at the  night king but perhaps at this point  Daenerys is raining a fire and blood is  even more dangerous and destructive than  the night King himself  and before long audiences will likely  see Daenerys standing in the real  ransacked version of the throne room  ready and determined to take whatever is  left of the Iron Throne itself check out  one of our newest videos right here plus  even more looper videos about Game of  Thrones are coming soon subscribe to our  YouTube channel and hit the bell so you  don't miss a single one  [Music]
 

